 C/WOLN:,NAME,DTRAN  /01.06.84/    . Terminate an output line
C===========================================================
C C/WOLN - "Write OUTPUT Line".  Wires M12 to the *OUTPUT*
C  FILE record, then falls through into C/WL.
C
C PUTLN - the same address under the name the P2C runtime
C  declaration `void putln() assembler' resolves to.  The
C  spelling NEWLINE cannot serve: it is an entry of FTNPRT
C  in library 21, which the loader searches ahead of libc.
C
C C/WL - terminate the current line on FILE @ M12.  Pushes
C  the LF char (PASEOLSY) into the buffer, then funnels into
C  C/PF to ship the data out.  Handles the page-eject case
C  for the line-printer.
C
C  Labelled in p_sys.asm: C/WL = FLUSHLIN, C/FL = *0600B.
C===========================================================
C Register convention (see FILE.md):
C   M12 = base of the FILE record being acted on
C   M1  = runtime constant table ([M1+8] = 1U, [M1+9] = integer-tag
C         mask, [M1+12] = positive-mantissa mask, [M1+25B] = MSB;
C         [M1+3..5] and [M1+35B..37B] are runtime scratch)
C   M13 = link register set by the calling VJM
C   M14 = secondary link (used inside packed-mode helpers)
 *OUTPUT*:,LC,30             . 30-word FILE record of OUTPUT
 PASEOLSY:,LC,1              . end-of-line char (ASCII LF)
 PASENDS*:,LC,1              . line-printer NEWLINE constant
 SPACE*:,LC,1                . ASCII space constant
 C/PF:,SUBP,                 . put f^ and advance the file
 P/PRINT:,SUBP,              . printf-like core (in p_print)
 C/TF:,SUBP,                 . truncate / rewrite the file
 C/PK:,SUBP,                 . pack ACC into the buffer slot
 C/FL:,SUBP,                 . forward decl, defined below
C===========================================
 PUTLN:,ENTRY,
C===========================================
 12,VTM,*OUTPUT*
C===========================================
 C/WL:,ENTRY,
C===========================================
 12,XTA,27B                  . ACC := FILE[23]
 1,AAX,10B
 ,U1A,C/FL                   . stdin/out -> the printer path
 ,UTC,PASEOLSY               . C := address of LF character
 ,XTA,
 12,WTC,                     . WT := FILE[0]
 ,ATX,                       . buffer[FILE[0]] := LF
 ,UJ,C/PF                    . fall through to C/PF
 SETPRINT:12,WTC,14B         . inner helper for C/WOLN trailer
 10,VTM,
 12,WTC,23B
 11,VTM,
 14,UJ,
C---------------------------------------------------------------
C C/FL - flush the buffered record to the line printer.  C/WL
C  falls in here for a stdin/stdout file, and C/PF jumps here
C  when it finds the same FILE[23] bit set.
 C/FL:,ENTRY,
 ,ITA,13                     . line-printer terminator path
 ,ITS,2                      . save M2
 12,XTS,
 ,ATI,2
 12,AEX,15B
 ,U1A,BLANKPG
 14,VJM,SETPRINT
 ,UTC,PASENDS*               . PASENDS* = page-feed control
 ,XTA,
 ,ASN,64-40
 11,ATX,
 DOPRINT:13,VJM,P/PRINT      . issue PRINT8 to flush record
 12,XTA,15B
 12,AEX,23B
 ,UZA,NEWPAGE
 13,VJM,C/TF                 . call C/TF helper
 PRTDONE:15,XTA,
 ,STI,2
 ,ATI,13                     . restore M13
 13,UJ,                      . return
 NEWPAGE:13,VJM,C/TF
 ,UTC,SPACE*
 ,XTA,
 12,WTC,
 ,ATX,                       . buffer[0] := space
 13,VTM,PRTDONE
 ,UJ,C/PF                    . issue final PUT
 BLANKPG:,UTC,PASENDS*       . blank-page path
 FILLLOOP:,XTA,
 2,ATX,
 2,UTM,1
 ,ITA,2
 12,AEX,1
 ,U1A,FILLLOOP
 14,VJM,C/PK                 . pack remainder
 14,VJM,SETPRINT             . header words
 ,UJ,DOPRINT                 . then print
 ,END,
